{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSXc7b4eeHVNSSY45rdK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need for the analysis phase. Let me summarize:\n\n**Conventions in repository:**\n- Controllers use `@PostMapping`, `@GetMapping` with `@PathVariable`\n- Success responses use `ResponseEntity` with appropriate `HttpStatus` (e.g., `HttpStatus.CREATED`)\n- Errors throw `ApiException` subclasses (`ConflictException`, `ResourceNotFoundException`) with `ErrorCode` enum values\n- Tests use `MockMvc` with assertions on status and jsonPath\n- The pattern is consistent: check existence → apply logic → save/throw → return response\n- Shipment data is immutable (data class) and stored in repository\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` - Must add the confirm endpoint\n2. `ApiError.kt` - Must add error code for invalid shipment state transition\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Must add tests for confirm endpoint\n\n**Risks:**\n- If not implementing idempotency correctly, retries could fail\n- If not persisting state change, confirmation won't persist across requests\n- If using wrong HTTP status codes, won't match API contract\n\n**Open questions:** None; the ticket is explicit about all required behaviors.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** (api package): Add error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION` to the `ErrorCode` enum. This will be used when attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** (shipment package): Add a new endpoint `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that:\n   - Takes the shipmentId from path variable\n   - Fetches the shipment from repository\n   - If not found: throw `ResourceNotFoundException` with `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`\n   - If found and status is `CANCELLED`: throw `ConflictException` with `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION`\n   - If found and status is `CREATED`: Create a new Shipment with status `CONFIRMED`, save it, return with `HttpStatus.OK`\n   - If found and status is `CONFIRMED`: Return it unchanged (idempotent) with `HttpStatus.OK`\n   - Return `ResponseEntity<Shipment>`\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** (test package): Add four new test methods:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED and returns it\n   - Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds and changes nothing (idempotency)\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with correct error code\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with correct error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Instead of adding a new error code, I considered reusing `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS` for the CANCELLED case, but this is semantically incorrect and would be confusing to API clients who need to distinguish between \"shipment already created\" and \"invalid state transition.\"\n- Instead of idempotency (returning OK for already CONFIRMED), I considered making it an error, but the ticket explicitly states \"a retry must not fail,\" so idempotency is required.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Caller receives | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|-----------------|-----------|\n| Confirm CREATED shipment | Shipment from repo | Updated shipment to repo | 200 OK + Shipment JSON | Normal flow, return ResponseEntity with OK |\n| Confirm already CONFIRMED shipment | Shipment from repo | Nothing | 200 OK + Shipment JSON (unchanged) | Idempotent, return existing shipment unchanged |\n| Confirm CANCELLED shipment | Shipment from repo | Nothing | 409 Conflict + error envelope | ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION |\n| Confirm non-existent shipment | Nothing | Nothing | 404 Not Found + error envelope | ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test: Confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED** - Creates shipment S-1, confirms it, verifies status changed to CONFIRMED and response is 200\n2. **Test: Confirm is idempotent on already CONFIRMED** - Creates and confirms S-2, confirms again, verifies 200 and status still CONFIRMED\n3. **Test: Reject confirming CANCELLED shipment** - Inserts CANCELLED shipment directly to repo, attempts confirm, verifies 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION error code\n4. **Test: Reject confirming non-existent shipment** - Attempts confirm on non-existent S-missing, verifies 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1042,"cache_read_input_tokens":18790,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1042},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95fa054d-3f4f-4624-90ad-ef22c04ab0be","uuid":"c4d5e239-9bfd-499a-8604-82659e0d3336","timestamp":"2026-09-26T18:31:50.628Z","request_id":"req_011CfSXc7A1uC86pjPuAej1S"}
